# CSS standards

## Scope and placement

- Put component styles in a single `{% stylesheet %}` tag in a section, block, or snippet.
- Do not put Liquid expressions inside `{% stylesheet %}`; pass dynamic setting values through CSS custom properties on the component markup.
- Keep styles used by multiple components in a shared asset instead of duplicating them.

```liquid
<div class="product-card" style="--card-gap: {{ block.settings.gap }}px">
  ...
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
.product-card {
  gap: var(--card-gap, 1rem);
}
{% endstylesheet %}
```

## Selectors and naming

- Prefer simple class selectors. Do not use IDs or broad element selectors for styling.
- Keep specificity low; avoid `!important` and use it only when an override cannot be expressed through the component styles.
- Use BEM-style names: `block`, `block__element`, and `block--modifier`, with dashes between words.
- Scope custom properties to the component unless they are genuinely shared. Define shared variables at `:root` and prefer theme colour settings over hard-coded colours.

## Responsive styles

- Write mobile-first rules and use `screen` media queries.
- Keep nesting to one level. Do not use the `&` nesting operator.
- Use pseudo-selectors sparingly and keep selectors readable.
